OK so push notifications can call `openRoom` but only one at a time per notification press. That's not the cause of 44 errors.

Let me look at this from yet another angle. The issue says "It gets triggered in the useRoomTimeline". Let me look at ALL the places in `useRoomTimeline` where the "Failed to mark room as read" error is logged:

```ts
const markAsRead = useCallback(async () => {
  if (!room) return;
  if (AppState.currentState !== "active") return;
  try {
    await room.markAsRead(ReceiptType.Read);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Failed to mark room as read:", error);
  }
}, [room]);
```

This is the only place the error is logged. The function gets called in two places: on mount or when the room changes, and when scrolling to the bottom. Since we're seeing exactly 44 errors matching the number of rooms, it's almost certainly happening during that initial effect when the component mounts.

On iPad specifically, something about the `Rooms` list in the sidebar must be triggering `useRoomTimeline` for every single room. The `RoomsListItem` doesn't directly render `RoomTimeline`, so there's got to be another component somewhere that's using this hook for the sidebar. Let me search for all usages of `useRoomTimeline` outside of the main `RoomTimeline.tsx` file to figure out what's actually running.

